# Spotify Connect mode — register an app at https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard
# then copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your Client ID.
#
# In the Spotify app settings, add these Redirect URIs (must match EXACTLY,
# including trailing slash rules — Vite serves at the bare origin):
#     http://127.0.0.1:5173/          (local dev — Spotify now requires 127.0.0.1, NOT localhost)
#     https://<your-deploy-host>/     (production website)
#     http://127.0.0.1:14565/callback (the Tauri desktop widget — loopback)
# Spotify rejects http://localhost AND custom schemes (skeuo://) as redirect
# URIs; use 127.0.0.1 loopback in both dev and desktop.
#
# No client secret is used — this is a public SPA using Authorization Code + PKCE.
# The desktop widget opens /authorize in the system browser and catches the
# return on a one-shot 127.0.0.1:14565 loopback listener (same PKCE flow).
VITE_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=

# ── macOS desktop build (signing + notarization) ─────────────────────────────
# Only needed to ship a signed .dmg (scripts/build-desktop.sh). NEVER commit
# real values — put them in a gitignored .env. Tauri reads these automatically.
#     APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY   "Developer ID Application: Your Name (TEAMID)"
#     APPLE_ID                 your-apple-id@example.com
#     APPLE_PASSWORD           an app-specific password (appleid.apple.com)
#     APPLE_TEAM_ID            10-char team id
